.TH DUK 1 "January 2025" "duk 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
duk \- TurningBull Data Utility Knife
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B duk
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fICOMMAND_ARGS\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBduk\fR is a CLI tool for downloading financial market data and performing data preprocessing. It provides various subcommands for accessing different types of financial data through APIs and performing common data transformations.

The general command line signature is \fBduk <subprogram> [optional arguments]\fR, where each subprogram acts like a stand-alone application within the duk interface.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable verbose logging to stderr
.TP
.BR \-\-help
Show help message and exit
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B tr
Download U.S. Treasury par yield curve rates. See \fBduk tr \-\-help\fR for detailed options.
.TP
.B ph
Download historical security price data. See \fBduk ph \-\-help\fR for detailed options.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Get help for the main command:
.B duk \-\-help
.TP
Get help for a specific subcommand:
.B duk tr \-\-help
.TP
.B duk ph \-\-help
.TP
Download latest Treasury rates:
.B duk tr
.TP
Download Treasury rates with verbose logging:
.B duk \-v tr
.TP
Download specific date Treasury rates:
.B duk tr \-\-date 2023\-12\-01
.TP
Download Treasury rates for last 5 days and save to file:
.B duk tr \-\-days 5 \-\-output
.TP
Download Treasury rates with interpolation:
.B duk tr \-\-interpolate
.TP
Download Treasury rates with bootstrap spot rates:
.B duk tr \-\-bootstrap\-spot\-rates
.TP
Download latest 5 days OHLC for AAPL:
.B duk ph AAPL
.TP
Download price history with date range:
.B duk ph AAPL \-\-start\-date 2023\-01\-01 \-\-end\-date 2023\-12\-31
.TP
Download OHLCV data with adjustments:
.B duk ph AAPL \-\-ohlcv \-\-adj
.TP
Download multiple tickers from file:
.B duk ph tickers.txt \-\-output
.TP
Download monthly aggregated data:
.B duk ph AAPL \-\-frequency monthly \-\-days 365
.SH TR SUBCOMMAND
The \fBtr\fR subcommand downloads U.S. Treasury par yield curve rates using the Financial Modeling Prep (FMP) API.

\fBNote:\fR An FMP API key is required. Place your key in \fIetc/.fmp_api.key\fR before running this command.

.SS TR Options
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-date " " \fIDATE\fR
Specific date to download (YYYY-MM-DD format)
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-start\-date " " \fIDATE\fR
Start date for date range (YYYY-MM-DD format)
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-end\-date " " \fIDATE\fR
End date for date range (YYYY-MM-DD format)
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-days " " \fINUMBER\fR
Number of days to download from start date (or latest date if no start date)
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output
Output to file instead of stdout
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-filename " " \fINAME\fR
Specify filename (overrides default naming)
.TP
.BR \-\-format " " {\fIcsv\fR|\fIjson\fR}
Output format (default: csv)
.TP
.BR \-D ", " \-\-directory " " \fIDIR\fR
Output directory (default: var)
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interpolate
Perform cubic spline interpolation
.TP
.BR \-\-interpolate\-interval " " {\fIday\fR|\fImonth\fR|\fIquarter\fR|\fIsemiannual\fR}
Interpolation interval (default: semiannual)
.TP
.BR \-\-bootstrap\-spot\-rates
Calculate bootstrap spot rates from par rates (implies --interpolate)

.SS TR Examples
.TP
Get latest Treasury data:
.B duk tr
.TP
Get data for last trading week:
.B duk tr \-\-days 5
.TP
Get specific date:
.B duk tr \-\-date 2023\-12\-01
.TP
Save last 30 days to default file:
.B duk tr \-\-days 30 \-\-output
.TP
Save to custom filename in JSON format:
.B duk tr \-\-days 10 \-\-filename rates_december \-\-format json \-\-output
.TP
Save to specific directory:
.B duk tr \-\-output \-\-directory ./data/treasury
.TP
Get data with cubic spline interpolation:
.B duk tr \-\-interpolate
.TP
Get data with bootstrap spot rates:
.B duk tr \-\-bootstrap\-spot\-rates
.SH PH SUBCOMMAND
The \fBph\fR subcommand downloads historical security price data using the Financial Modeling Prep (FMP) API.

\fBNote:\fR An FMP API key is required. Place your key in \fIetc/.fmp_api.key\fR before running this command.

.SS PH Options
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-start\-date " " \fIDATE\fR
Start date for date range (YYYY-MM-DD format)
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-end\-date " " \fIDATE\fR
End date for date range (YYYY-MM-DD format)
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-days " " \fINUMBER\fR
Number of observations to return (default: 5)
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output
Output to file instead of stdout
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-filename " " \fIFILENAME\fR
Specify filename (overrides default naming)
.TP
.BR \-\-format " " {\fIcsv\fR|\fIjson\fR}
Output format (default: csv)
.TP
.BR \-D ", " \-\-directory " " \fIDIRECTORY\fR
Output directory (default: var)
.TP
.BR \-\-frequency " " {\fIdaily\fR|\fIweekly\fR|\fImonthly\fR|\fIquarterly\fR|\fIsemiannual\fR|\fIannual\fR}
Data frequency (default: daily)
.TP
.BR \-\-ohlc
Include Open, High, Low, Close prices (default)
.TP
.BR \-\-hlc
Include High, Low, Close prices
.TP
.BR \-\-ohlcv
Include Open, High, Low, Close, Volume
.TP
.BR \-\-vol
Include Volume
.TP
.BR \-\-adj
Include adjusted close prices
.TP
.BR \-\-div
Include dividend data
.TP
.BR \-\-split
Include stock split data

.SS PH Examples
.TP
Get latest 5 days OHLC for AAPL:
.B duk ph AAPL
.TP
Get last 30 days with volume:
.B duk ph AAPL \-\-days 30 \-\-ohlcv
.TP
Get specific date range:
.B duk ph AAPL \-\-start\-date 2023\-01\-01 \-\-end\-date 2023\-12\-31
.TP
Get data with adjustments:
.B duk ph AAPL \-\-adj \-\-div \-\-split
.TP
Save multiple tickers to file:
.B duk ph tickers.txt \-\-output
.TP
Get monthly aggregated data:
.B duk ph AAPL \-\-frequency monthly \-\-days 365 \-\-format json \-\-output
.SH FILES
.TP
.I etc/.fmp_api.key
Financial Modeling Prep API key file (required for tr and ph subcommands)
.TP
.I var/duk.log
Default log file location
.TP
.I var/
Default output directory for saved files
.SH ENVIRONMENT
The program respects standard Python environment variables and uses the system's Python path for module resolution.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 1
General error (invalid arguments, API errors, etc.)
.SH AUTHOR
TurningBull
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR python (1),
.BR pip (1)

For detailed documentation, see the files in the \fIdoc/\fR directory of the source distribution.